{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's motion and perception capabilities, separating motion commands from sensor events. The specification enforces conservative, safe exploration: random_walk is used in clear, non-obstacle states; move_forward is only allowed in a short commit state; obstacle events force explicit, one-shot turn-based recovery with no ambiguous choices; recovery states only allow a single turn direction based on obstacle side; forward/random_walk are never enabled in obstacle states; recovery must complete before exploration resumes.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for motion and perception to reflect open-loop actuation and asynchronous sensing.",
    "Specification automaton encodes strict safety: obstacle events preempt forward/random_walk, force explicit turn recovery, and only allow resumption of exploration after recovery and path_clear."
  ],
